  ],
  "text": "The Sun is stripping the air off Mars right now, and it has been for billions of years. Earth sits in exactly the same wind and loses nothing. The reason is six thousand kilometres beneath you, and it is liquid metal. Moving metal makes a magnetic field. The whole planet works as one giant dynamo. That field reaches tens of thousands of kilometres out into space. So the solar wind arrives, hits it, and slides straight around us. The few particles that get through are funnelled down at the poles. So every aurora you have seen is the shield leaking, visibly. Mars had a field like ours once. Then its core cooled and stopped moving. No moving metal, no shield. Its air is out there somewhere, blown downwind. The air in your lungs is still here because deep down, metal is still turning. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
